{
  "case_id": "2021-21-234",
  "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Melanie L. Bostwick)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-234",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95ee156d9f71-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BOSTWICK: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Our nation's veterans benefits system is intended to be strongly and uniquely pro-claimant. In this non-adversarial system, veterans enjoy distinct procedural protections, and review of otherwise final decisions for Clear and Unmistakable Error, or CUE, is one of those unique protections. It prevents the agency's obvious errors from depriving veterans of the benefits to which their service entitles them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-234",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95ee156d9f71-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So you think it's just like an unfortunate part of that, of -- of something, of --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2021-21-234",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95ee156d9f71-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He's not sound if it was that. Was it that? No."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. BOSTWICK",
      "case_id": "2021-21-234",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95ee156d9f71-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So let's see if he fits in B, and the answer is we're not sure, but maybe we are, but, regardless, the reg didn't copy the words \"and was not aggravated by service.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2021-21-234",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95ee156d9f71-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But I think, Ms. Bostwick, that that's kind of not the issue. I mean, the issue is that there was a regulation that said that, and the question is what effect that regulation had."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2021-21-234",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95ee156d9f71-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But why -- why isn't that the issue? I mean, you're trying to make this a lot simpler than it actually is. You have one interpretation of the concept of error: Is it objectively erroneous? The government has another: Was there an adjudicative error? And we have to decide which one is the correct interpretation. How do we decide?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2021-21-234",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95ee156d9f71-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, can we go back to your point that this statute is not about adjudicator error, it's about error in the decision, and that's the language of the statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice THOMAS",
      "case_id": "2021-21-234",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95ee156d9f71-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But how can we be sure that Congress codified your understanding, whatever that is, of CUE?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2021-21-234",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95ee156d9f71-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do we do with Professor Mascott's amicus brief, for example, in which she quite rightly points out that we don't normally think of judicial interpretations as changes in the law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (MR. YANG)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-234",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95ee156d9f71-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It might in some sense be understandable, justified maybe even, but why can't that be fairly described as clear and unmistakable error to the extent it rests on, its analysis depends upon, a clear misinterpretation of the statute, as Justice Breyer outlined?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2021-21-234",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95ee156d9f71-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just want to make sure -- I think I asked this question imprecisely to Ms. Bostwick -- but was there any congressional suggestion that this situation, in other words, a reg that had been in existence before is later declared invalid, would itself be the trigger for retroactive benefits? Are you aware of anything one way or the other?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2021-21-234",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95ee156d9f71-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 79,
        "start": 79
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My question is really about the Secretary review. Is that a real thing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (MS. BOSTWICK)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-234",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95ee156d9f71-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 84,
        "start": 83
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Second, in speaking about supplemental claims, there was a suggestion that one could bring such a claim with cumulative evidence or with a legal error. Neither of those is correct. It is available only for new and relevant evidence, formally known as new and material evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-234",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95ee156d9f71f1f428cb296f97e6bfd52142271612cd32d708dbd001fb1b2430",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95ee156d9f71-0003-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:16 a.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
